WEBVTT

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.690
Yumiko-chan.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.040
Here we go!

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.910
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.400
In that case...

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.630
I did it!

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.110
No way.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.440
Koyomi.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.030
I did it!

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.000
Koyomi!

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.320
It's futile.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.480
You have no chance of winning.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.880
6 hours earlier

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.310
This should be far enough...

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.870
Jeez!

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.660
Hey!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.840
What was that just now?

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.560
What a horrible day.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.640
Someone's trying to kill me,

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.500
and the entire lower half of my body is catching way too much air.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.720
Take that!

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.470
Ichinose Yumiko wears striped panties!

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:22.640
Yeah!

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.980
If you want to see them so bad,

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.180
why don't you spend the rest of your life with them stuck to your face?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.980
I did nothing wrong!

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.990
You went too far.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.210
You stand out.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.220
If you don't try to get along with those around you a bit better,

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.680
you won't be able to make any friends.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:51.500
I don't want to make friends with people of such a low level!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.510
I'm at my wit's end.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.070
Elementary school is not where I belong.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.580
Today is when I put my plan into action.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.910
Yumiko, what's wrong?

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.910
Shouldn't you still be at school?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.780
Mother...

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:33.110
I'll bid farewell to this worthless world and become a mage.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.930
That is my plan.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:40.440
What started all this

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.670
were the notes I happened to find, left by my great-grandfather,

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:47.020
and this staff, named Kerykeion.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:51.800
At the beginning of his notes, it says

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.430
that if one cannot see magic, that one will not be able to read the notes.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:00.030
And when I continued reading, I understood

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.900
exactly what I am.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.590
I am a natural-born mage,

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:11.010
inheriting the blood and talent of my great-grandfather, Karl Cristbarth.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:18.630
These purple eyes and silver hair of mine are all proof of that.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.610
But there's one problem.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:27.770
There's nothing in here that tells you how to use magic at all!

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.850
It seems that you have to construct a Code, but...

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.540
What does that even mean?

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.280
However, there is a hint.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.910
A school that will teach you magic...

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:44.000
If I go there, I should be able to understand what a Code is.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:51.000
Anehara Cross School of Magic

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.310
The Anehara Cross School of Magic.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.720
Misa-san!

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.460
Anehara Misa-san!

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.970
Stop that. It's embarrassing.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.760
You're a kid, aren't you?

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.220
Don't just say "you" all the time.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.680
My name is Morishita Koyomi.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.660
I might be smaller than you, but I'm a lot older, Soshiro-kun!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.870
Older, huh?

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.540
I wonder where Misa-san is...

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.680
She's just shopping for dinner, so I don't think she went too far.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:23.500
Wouldn't it have been better if we had waited at home?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.090
You're right.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.680
I guess we should go back.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:30.280
Besides, what do you need my sister for, anyway?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.010
There's something I have to ask her about magic.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.360
Magic?

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:35.950
What are you saying?

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.630
You really are just a kid.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:39.340
No, I'm not!

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.770
Magic really does exist.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.360
Then show me.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.790
So you were just lying, then?

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.640
I wasn't!

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:50.130
Give me a cell phone!

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.520
Me, too!

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:57.990
Watch this.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.770
Concentrate. Concentrate...

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:08.560
I'll change this Code into the one magic that I know.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.680
I'll restructure it into that other Code.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.510
Ouch...

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.580
Soshiro-kun!

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.830
Huh? Why am I buying a cell phone?

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.390
Sorry, I'd like to return this.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:27.560
Ow...

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.050
Are you okay?

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.120
But you did see the magic, didn't you?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.160
This wash basin... You planned this, didn't you?

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.620
How was that magic? If anything, it was a magic trick!

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.370
It was magic!

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.330
There's no way magic actually exists!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.570
Don't get so mad-

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:42.860
Shut up!

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:43.710
Wait!

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:44.570
Don't run away!

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.940
If I don't hurry...

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:59.500
And if I don't figure out what a Code is before he finds me,

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.970
I'll...

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.760
be killed.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.270
Joyeux Noël, mademoiselle.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.990
Do the people of this country not respond to greetings?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.990
Good afternoon.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.340
You have a nice Code.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:28.370
As to be expected from one with Cristbarth's blood running through them.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.200
Who are you?

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:37.000
I guess those of your household, when asking another's name, don't first state their own?

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:41.020
Ichinose Yumiko Cristina.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:44.520
Jean-Jacques Guibarthez.

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:47.710
Did you need something from me?

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:50.010
I'll take your staff.

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.510
This is mine!

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:58.220
I have some business with the Sorceress's Library sealed within that staff by Cristbarth.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.330
Now, hand it over.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.340
I refuse!

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:06.810
Understanding the strength of an enemy is also a skill, mademoiselle.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:17.180
The next one won't miss.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.340
<i>No!</i>

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:29.680
A police booth.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:31.520
I'm saved.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.710
But how can I explain the situation?

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.890
I'm being chased by some weird mage?

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:44.950
He won't believe that.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.400
What's wrong, miss?

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.920
N-Nothing at all!

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:54.720
I can only depend on myself.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:58.130
I need the power to fight.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.500
If I can make it to the Anehara Cross School of Magic,

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:04.000
then I'm sure I'll be able to learn to use magic!

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.230
P-Please help me!

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:15.680
Until a second ago, customers were flying at me, but now, they've suddenly stopped coming.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.460
At this rate, my sales...

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.900
My quota!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.510
That's weird...

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:24.950
The Code I constructed to raise people's desire to spend was completely erased.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.450
I wonder what the cause was.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.860
You don't know the reason...

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:32.570
I'm finished.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:35.370
Everything's over!

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:37.250
No need to worry.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.080
My sales!

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:45.610
Here I go.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.600
Transmit!

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:54.920
Sell them to me!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.420
All the phones in this store!

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.030
Me, too!

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:58.110
I'll buy some, too!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:02.490
Wow.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.770
Way to go!

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.550
As a bonus, I upped the effectiveness a bit.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:09.010
Now you'll be able to reach your quota, right?

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:11.700
Thank you very much!

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.410
Is there anything I can do for you?

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:17.860
I'm already getting paid quite a bit, so it's okay. Don't worry about it.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.890
But I guess, if you insist,

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.870
maybe I'll take that.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.880
<b>Anehara</b>

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.480
Is this really the place?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:38.390
It's almost like a haunted house.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:45.000
For your destination to be Anehara... I guess fate is in full swing.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:52.480
Did you enjoy that game of hide-and-seek?

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.090
I wonder if Misa-san'll get back soon.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.080
Oh, is that...

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:20.110
What is it?

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:24.290
Okay, playtime is over.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:27.760
Will you give me the staff, or will you go to your grave?

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.370
You get to pick.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.600
Giving away the staff means giving up on magic.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.820
And I'll be back to the same old stupid thing every day.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.380
I don't want that, even if I die!

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.880
This staff means everything to me!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.620
I won't hand it over to anyone!

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:46.180
I see.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:47.640
In that case...

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.150
I'm going to get killed.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.600
Yumiko-chan!

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:54.350
You must be Yumiko-chan!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.480
You're Yumiko-chan, right?

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:56.730
You're Yumiko-chan!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.750
Who are you?

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.680
Why do you know my name?

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.650
You're so small and cute!

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.120
Hey!

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.910
I don't know you at all!

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.170
That's true.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:10.170
You're right.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:13.000
You don't know about me at all yet.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.290
What's all the noise about?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.130
Your hair was cute when you were younger, too.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.510
How nice...

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:22.440
You had silver hair when you were younger, too.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:25.790
I guess now that I think about it, it's pretty obvious, but I like it anyway!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:26.980
What's with you?

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:28.100
Go away!

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.010
Shoo shoo!

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.410
You know her?

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:32.090
Yep.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.230
We're friends.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:37.730
But I guess this is Yumiko-chan's first time meeting me.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.750
Since we just met, I guess we're friends, right?

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.040
What are you talking about?

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.010
You done talking?

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:45.820
Huh?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.420
I didn't say anything.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:49.780
Not you, Soshiro-kun.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.970
It's nice you got to meet her before you die.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:56.470
I'll kill you with Cristbarth's own Code.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:02.290
If thou art the one who moves time, then I have come back through it.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:07.060
If thou art the one who fights against time, then I am the one who moves it.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:07.050
That spell... It can't be.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:11.610
Wax and wane, until the tremors calm,

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:15.050
for thine is the clock that I shall wind.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.960
W-Wait a second!

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:28.260
A wash basin?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.440
Jeez, another magic trick?

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:34.040
What are you doing, sending the Code of Swords at someone?

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:37.020
To be able to restructure my Code in an instant...

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.380
I see. You must be Anehara Misa.

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.520
Anehara Misa?

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:44.520
Anehara Cross School of Magic

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.050
This girl is Anehara?

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:49.360
You have a good Code.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:53.470
You do indeed have the blood of Anehara Kenjuro running through you.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.800
Um, Misa-san is...

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.280
But next time, it won't go the same way.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:00.170
Yumiko-chan, get back.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:03.310
Do you think you can oppose me?

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:09.420
I don't know, but I don't think what you've done is good.

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.680
So, then you'll put your life on the line?

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:14.520
I'm scared. I want to run away,

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:16.270
but I've decided that when it matters,

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:19.460
I won't run away, and I'll stand my ground.

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:25.060
My legs might be shaking, but that's fine.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:26.210
That's the way it's going to be.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:30.440
I can't really say it correctly, but... Uh, you know...

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:31.500
Yeah!

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:34.820
At first, it may have just been chance, but depending on what you choose,

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:37.460
you can change chance into fate!

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:41.460
That's a nice mindset you have there, but you won't be alive for long.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.460
Uh... Um...

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.010
Since we've run this far, we should be okay.

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.850
Huh? Yumiko-chan?

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:07.930
Cold!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.420
Oh, my. You followed me?

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:27.430
It might have been better for you to have gone to Anehara Misa, though.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.930
Anehara Misa...

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:36.720
She looks a lot different than the mages I had pictured.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.950
That goofy look she had on her face...

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:42.960
Depending on what you choose, you can change chance into fate!

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:45.000
That's not true at all!

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:52.740
My fate was sealed the moment I was born with these eyes and this hair.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:57.580
Thanks to them, I was constantly stared at and made fun of.

00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:00.020
I never had a friend.

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:03.550
Ichinose-san looks like a doll. So pretty.

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:05.270
But she's kind of scary.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.790
She gives me the creeps.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:10.130
But I'm not lonely at all.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:13.370
After all, I'm special!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:14.540
I don't need friends.

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.540
Yeah, friends.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.970
I won't be fooled!

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:23.660
Besides, how did she know my name when it was the first time we'd met?

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.520
I'm sure she's just like Guibarthez.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:29.280
She must be planning something!

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.750
What's wrong?

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:41.200
Wh-What is that?

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:07.480
We're taking this chance to run.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:20.540
No way...

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:34.480
Hide here.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:48.250
I can't...

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.250
die here!

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:56.490
Think back.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:59.330
You should have seen with your own eyes... How to use magic,

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:01.440
how to construct a Code.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:06.780
If thou art the one who moves time, then I have come back through it.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:12.440
If thou art the one who fights against time, then I am the one who moves it.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:16.540
Wax and wane, until the tremors calm,

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:19.270
for thine is the clock that I shall wind.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:24.530
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:47.550
This is magic?

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.940
I can see it. I can see it!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:04.210
The world was filled with Codes all along!

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:08.660
To defeat my familiar...

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:16.340
The Code I just felt, that was Cristbarth's Code.

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:21.390
You really are his descendant if you mastered it just by seeing it once.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:22.330
Guibarthez.

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:27.190
I'm sure you could have become a wonderful mage if you had continued to practice,

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:28.770
but I'm out of time.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:31.360
You will die here.

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:34.110
Farewell!

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:44.030
Yumiko-chan!

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:51.500
Misa-san!

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:52.570
Thank god.

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:53.830
I finally found you!

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:57.810
I have no clue who you are, but I'm not very impressed.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:00.330
You're bullying such a small girl.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.850
Santa Claus?

00:22:13.110 --> 00:22:15.070
Merry Christmas.

00:23:46.390 --> 00:23:50.450
Six years from now, that's where I should have been originally.

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:54.180
It's the story of the day I made the first step.

00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:58.590
That day, I met a mage.

00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:04.690
TV Course
Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:07.070
TV Course
Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou
Lesson 1: Modern-Day Magic

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:11.200
Hello, I'm Morishita Koyomi!

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:13.770
How was the anime? I'm Anehara Misa.

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:17.070
Hey, Misa-san, what is this segment?

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:20.500
This is the Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou TV Course,

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:24.150
where we make the many series-specific terms and matters related to the show

00:24:24.150 --> 00:24:26.570
that we don't have adequate time to explain

00:24:26.570 --> 00:24:29.580
easy to understand.

00:24:29.580 --> 00:24:32.980
I see... Th-That's a lot of responsibility.

00:24:32.980 --> 00:24:35.110
Koyomi's gonna try her best!

00:24:35.110 --> 00:24:38.280
So, what are you going to teach us today?

00:24:38.280 --> 00:24:42.890
Let's tell them about magic, since it's in the title.

00:24:40.350 --> 00:25:09.130
What is magic?

00:24:42.890 --> 00:24:45.360
Koyomi, to put it simply, what is magic?

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:49.130
M-M-Magic's... Uh...

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:51.380
It's all <i>buzz </i>and then <i>zoom!</i>

00:24:51.380 --> 00:24:54.880
Oh, my. Well, how about I explain it?

00:24:54.880 --> 00:24:59.050
Magic is something that inserts different laws into our world,

00:24:59.050 --> 00:25:02.890
rewriting the conventional laws of physics, causing different phenomena to occur.

00:25:02.890 --> 00:25:05.940
Teacher, I didn't really get any of that.

00:25:05.940 --> 00:25:08.340
Then let's go at it step-by-step.

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:11.310
First, what is a Code exactly?

00:25:09.130 --> 00:25:13.340
Code

00:25:11.310 --> 00:25:13.500
Right! That, I know.

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:16.050
Code = Spell

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:14.770
It's a spell.

00:25:14.770 --> 00:25:15.790
That's right.

00:25:15.790 --> 00:25:19.830
A magical spell is called a Code in this world.

00:25:19.830 --> 00:25:23.970
Using that to cause paranormal phenomena is called magic.

00:25:23.970 --> 00:25:28.890
To start off, Classical Magic uses your own body as a launching point.

00:25:24.060 --> 00:25:31.150
Classical Magic

00:25:28.890 --> 00:25:33.430
I see. Then what's the Modern-Day Magic that you use?

00:25:33.430 --> 00:25:37.780
Modern-Day Magic uses special programs, with which computers, networks, and the like

00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:47.330
Modern-Day Magic

00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:44.090
replace humans and the nervous system to process and execute Codes.

00:25:44.090 --> 00:25:46.630
Koyomi, did you understand?

00:25:46.630 --> 00:25:48.400
Um... Um...

00:25:47.380 --> 00:26:07.060
What is magic?

00:25:48.400 --> 00:25:52.380
Classical Magic passes electricity through the body to create magic,

00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:58.360
and Modern-Day Magic uses computers and... and...

00:25:59.010 --> 00:26:02.480
Unlike everyone at home, I guess Koyomi'll need a review.

00:26:03.220 --> 00:26:05.080
See you next week!

00:26:07.060 --> 00:26:10.030
The End
